IOC Containers:
---------------
IOC containers are the responsible for creating beans and managing the life cycle of the beans. They are also
responsible for dependencies injection in the spring beans. they also manage the configuration of the data.

Two types of IOC Container:
1. BeanFactory.
2. Application Context.

1. BeanFactory:
-> Basic IOC. 
-> Lazy Loading. Beans are created and managed in IOC when requested.
-> When memory is the constarin use bean factory.
-> Simple and light weight only supports basic IOC container features, No support of AOP, No Internalisation, Event Handling etc/

2. Appliation COntext:
-> This is widely used now a days. it is feature rich IOC.
-> It creates all the beans while start up. 
-> It supports internalization.
-> Event Handling.
-> Supports the AOP, Resource loadimg from filepaths, class paths etc.
-> Automatic wiring Is fully Supported.
-> Provides multiple Implememation ways:
1. classpathxmlapplicationcontext.
2. AnnotationConfigApplicationCOntext.
 
