Scopes of Bean in Spring:
=========================
In Spring, the scope of a bean defines the lifecycle and visibility of that bean within the Spring container. It determines 
how many instances of the bean are created and how they are shared across the application. 

1. @scope("singleton")
-> It creates a single instance of bean. No matter what how many beans are there it only gives you the same bean.
2. @scope("prototype")
-> It creates a new object of bean every time you request for the bean.
3. @scope("request")
->  A new bean instance is created for each HTTP request.
4. @session("session")
-> One bean instance per HTTP session.

